{"doc_id": "doc7894", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Originally, Spielberg suggested Harrison Ford; Lucas resisted the idea, since he had already cast the actor in American Graffiti, Star Wars and The Empire Strikes Back, and did not want Ford to become known as his \"Bobby De Niro\" (in reference to the fact that fellow director Martin Scorsese regularly casts Robert De Niro in his films). During an intensive casting process, Lucas and Spielberg auditioned many actors, and finally cast actor Tom Selleck as Indiana Jones. Shortly afterward pre-production began in earnest on Raiders of the Lost Ark. However, CBS refused to release Selleck from his contractual commitment to Magnum, P.I. (which was gradually gaining momentum in the ratings), forcing him to turn down the role. One of CBS's concerns was that shooting for Magnum P.I. conflicted with shooting for Raiders, both of which were to begin about the same time. However, Selleck was to say later in an interview that shooting for Magnum P.I. was delayed and did not actually begin until shooting for Raiders had concluded.", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 424499624, "similarity": 0.9942196531791907, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "69cb2fe46e18e28f67abb0e57aed38c4e2fefe244eceaec877160cdeeabb3860", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Tom Selleck", "matched_aliases": ["Tom Selleck"], "query_id": "test217", "question_hash": "eb8cd8f28a57d6167ed44b77293f411709e8b18d55a3a70b9d14ee0f9a8517f1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "dcef4fb1e602ab7f89ed99f2ef77123eb065545afbd1feb4f5faf58915e89192", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1058012109, "similarity": 0.05245901639344262, "source_content_hash": "8cf283678ba008d3e7c5b0f9161b01da5a417200a8384f4dfb239ee5569501cb", "source_hash": "9fc3ed0e4fe9d77cd9d7fc940fb10d6bef0d8f1842f26ce7f6c0f469e0948eda", "target_answer":