{"doc_id": "doc38533", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Greek writers of natural history were convinced of the reality of unicorns, which they believed lived in India, a distant and fabulous realm for them. The earliest description is from Ctesias, who in his book Indika (\"On India\") described them as wild asses, fleet of foot, having a horn a cubit and a half (700 mm, 28 inches) in length, and colored white, red and black. Aristotle must be following Ctesias when he mentions two one-horned animals, the oryx (a kind of antelope) and the so-called \"Indian ass\". Strabo says that in the Caucasus there were one-horned horses with stag-like heads. Pliny the Elder mentions the oryx and an Indian ox (perhaps a rhinoceros) as one-horned beasts, as well as \"a very fierce animal called the monoceros which has the head of the stag, the feet of the elephant, and the tail of the boar, while the rest of the body is like that of the horse; it makes a deep lowing noise, and has a single black horn, which projects from the middle of its forehead, two cubits [900 mm, 35 inches] in length\". In On the Nature of Animals (Περὶ Ζῴων Ἰδιότητος, De natura animalium), Aelian, quoting Ctesias, adds that India produces also a one-horned horse (iii. 41; iv. 52), and says (xvi. 20) that the monoceros (Greek: μονόκερως) was sometimes called cartazonos (Greek: καρτάζωνος), which may be a form of the Arabic karkadann, meaning \"rhinoceros\".", "reason": "near_duplicate_of_source", "seed": 1484644863, "similarity": 0.9567642956764296, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e6671a7422676f90491de0644edffe9b5840be50a0087508d29a1d26a94c64df", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Greek writers of natural history", "matched_aliases": ["Greek writers of natural history"], "query_id": "test1101", "question_hash": "b7c25b3f1fabd59be7b7f6af83bbee8d5c66b78a17e52df3560c23baa000421c", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "c2023b1d420933a18bed2a676d01bfc8da4ddac34a1e05af3d1b67bda26dd1c8", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1383031507, "similarity": 0.03923205342237062, "source_content_hash": "be33ca8705f7170ba4c3af133fd436e613de2452b3732f58a1220e1c0a6208b9", "source_hash": "e80110000c92b2b16ce945c128a4baf5a1bda15b1e6acc8caee88e672e866a35", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7cd138b014cd55a5524c4bf6fc96686d51623c3651d541b5ebc3b5fbd5ac079a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
